    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 18,
      "title": "Drift Over Time",
      "description": "Both gauges. A step change that persists means a recon run found a real gap; a sawtooth means it is being corrected each night.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "noValue": "no data",
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "warden_ledger_recon_drift_usd",
          "legendFormat": "ledger drift"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "warden_ledger_recon_hold_drift_usd",
          "legendFormat": "hold drift"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Authorization Chokepoint",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Verdicts by Enforcement State",
      "description": "The `enforced` label distinguishes AUTHORIZE_PAYMENT_ENFORCED=true from the shadow mode. A wall of DENY at enforced=false is what the flip would have produced before kya.py started granting a default L2 policy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "noValue": "no data",
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (verdict, enforced) (rate(warden_payment_authorization_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{verdict}} / enforced={{enforced}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Which checks inside authorize_payment() actually evaluate. `not_evaluated` means the check allowed without assessing anything \u2014 the Budget Guardian returns that for every tenant with agentic commerce off, which on 2026-08-19 was all of them. A chokepoint whose second check never fires is a one-check chokepoint; this panel is how you notice before flipping AUTHORIZE_PAYMENT_ENFORCED.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 910,
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (check, outcome) (rate(warden_payment_authorization_check_total[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "{{check}} / {{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Chokepoint \u2014 which checks evaluate",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Offer Signature Verification",
      "description": "warden_marketplace_offer_signature_total{result,enforced} \u2014 MARKETPLACE_REQUIRE_SIGNED_OFFERS turns this from observe-and-count into reject.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
